Title: check_figures anchors break on prose re-wrap: match across line breaks
Created: 2026-09-01
Author: MinhHaDuong

--- log ---
2026-09-01T11:30Z MinhHaDuong created

--- body ---
## Context
`bench/check_figures.py` anchors match against the file's raw text, so an
anchored phrase split by an ordinary prose re-wrap stops matching and reports
STALE with the figure unchanged. It fired twice on 2026-09-01 during the 0091
round-4/round-5 body edits (`of {} hits both arms return`, `so {} moved onto
the match`), and the workaround — keeping every figure-bearing phrase on one
physical line — is now folklore in two agent prompts, which is the tell that
the guard is fighting the document format instead of reading it.

## Actions
Normalize whitespace (newlines included) on both the anchor and the scanned
text before matching, preserving the positional-slot semantics and the
duplicate-anchor separation the file's comments defend.

## Test
Red first: an existing green anchor re-wrapped across a line break must stay
green after the fix and be shown red against the pre-fix matcher.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] a line break inside an anchored phrase no longer produces STALE
- [ ] the positional/dedup semantics keep their existing tests green
- [ ] `make check` green; the one-physical-line folklore removed from prose
